@model AncinInsaat.Models.ProjectDetailViewModel

@* Image Gallery, redesigned as premium Category Cards (Gallery Category
   Cards redesign, 2026-08-04 — inspired by, not copying,
   Inspirationals/Folkart's Orion gallery). Reuses _FilterDropdown.cshtml
   as-is for the category selector — restyled via #project-gallery-scoped
   CSS only, so Projects/Index's two dropdowns are untouched — and the
   shared Media Viewer (_MediaViewer.cshtml, site.js) for the lightbox, same
   as the previous flat-grid version. Every gallery image renders exactly
   once, in category order (Exterior, then Interior, then Social Areas —
   ProjectsController.GalleryCategorySortOrder), as its own card. "Tüm
   Görseller" (2026-08-04 fix — was only ever showing one card per
   category) shows every card, in that same order; picking a category
   shows only that category's cards. data-media-viewer-group-category
   holds each card's own category group; data-media-viewer-group starts
   equal to it (cards render visible-by-default, matching "Tüm Görseller"
   being the default selection) and site.js repoints it to "gallery-all" or
   back to the category group whenever the filter changes, so the Media
   Viewer — which resolves group membership from that attribute at click
   time rather than baking it in at page load — always opens on the
   correct combined-or-category list with no duplicate entries. Filtering
   is scoped, single-instance JS in site.js ("Project Gallery — Category
   Cards"), deliberately not sharing the generic Filter Dropdown module:
   that one early-exits whenever [data-project-grid] is absent, which would
   leave this page's _FilterDropdown.cshtml instance inert. Every project
   with 1+ named categories gets this dropdown/category-card treatment
   (Nlatis Gallery revision, 2026-08-10 — previously a project with exactly
   one named category fell back to a plain ungrouped grid with no dropdown,
   since there was "nothing meaningful to filter"; changed generically, not
   as an Nlatis-specific slug check, once a real single-category project —
   Nlatis, "Exterior" only — needed its one category offered as a real
   dropdown entry alongside "Tüm Görseller", matching every other project's
   Gallery interface). A project with zero named categories (every image's
   Category left null, e.g. La Via AVM — see BuildKuyuluAvmImages) still
   gets the same card treatment: every image renders as one ungrouped set,
   and _FilterDropdown's Options list is empty, so its menu offers only its
   built-in "Tüm Görseller" entry (Consistency Revisions, 2026-08-06). The
   old plain-grid fallback (.project-gallery/.gallery-thumb, previously
   reached only when a project had exactly one named category) is now
   unreachable and has been removed.

   Block / Apartment Type chip rows (La Fiore Karabağ 2. Etap Gallery pilot,
   2026-08-06) — ONLY for this project; every other project's images leave
   GalleryImageModel.Block/ApartmentType null, so both rows below simply
   don't render for them (no slug check needed anywhere). Each row lists the
   distinct values present across ALL gallery images up front; site.js hides
   individual chips (and the whole row, when fewer than 2 remain) as the
   category/block selection narrows the visible set, so a chip is only ever
   offered when it would actually do something. Each .gallery-card below
   carries data-gallery-block/data-gallery-apartment-type so site.js can
   filter without another server round-trip.

   Gallery videos (Gallery video support, 2026-08-09) — any GalleryImageModel
   with VideoUrl set renders as a video card (poster thumbnail + Play icon,
   same card shell) instead of a Media Viewer trigger; Play opens the shared
   video modal Concept's video slides already use (site.js, broadened
   trigger selector). Purely data-driven off ProjectImage.VideoPath — no
   per-project code, works identically for every project's Gallery.

   Nav arrows (2026-08-04 refinement): .project-gallery-nav-group's two
   .history-nav-btn buttons (data-gallery-prev/next) sit beneath
   [data-gallery-cards] and scroll it by one card via site.js — reusing the
   same button and disabled-state styling as the History Carousel/Floor
   Plans/Projects Showcase, alongside (not instead of) the track's native
   drag/swipe/wheel scrolling. Only rendered in this Category Cards branch;
   the plain-grid fallback below has no horizontal track to scroll. *@

@if (Model.GalleryImages.Count == 0)
{
    <p class="projects-grid-empty">Bu proje için galeri görselleri yakında eklenecek.</p>
}
else
{
    <div class="project-gallery-header">
        <h2 id="project-gallery-heading" class="sr-only">Galeri</h2>
        <p class="project-gallery-title" aria-hidden="true">GALERİ</p>

        <partial name="_FilterDropdown" model="@(new AncinInsaat.Models.FilterDropdownModel
        {
            FilterKey = "gallery-category",
            Placeholder = "Tüm Görseller",
            Options = Model.GalleryCategories.Select(category => category.Label).ToList()
        })" />
    </div>

    @* Category Cards under "Tüm Görseller" (Nysa Gold Residence reference
       redesign, 2026-08-07; rolled out to every project, 2026-08-08) —
       replaces the immediate merged grid with one static card per gallery
       category, side by side. Static row/wrap layout (2026-08-28 revision —
       replaces the previous continuously-looping marquee, which duplicated
       this same set 6× and animated it via CSS transform; see site.css/
       site.js history for that removed implementation). Each real card
       renders exactly once — no duplication, no auto-scroll.

       Picker cards render as plain .gallery-card markup (same <img>/
       overlay/title structure as every Interior/Exterior card below), so
       they share the exact same width, height, border radius, typography
       and spacing — no separate card design. Clicking one does not route
       through the dropdown's selectOption/setCategory (which would swap
       this picker for the filtered grid); site.js instead opens the
       existing Media Viewer directly, scoped to every image in that
       category, so "Tüm Görseller" itself never navigates away. The
       dropdown and applyFilters/setCategory architecture are otherwise
       completely untouched — selecting a category from the dropdown still
       swaps to the filtered grid exactly as before. *@
    @* Only meaningful when there's at least one named category to pick from
       — a project with zero named categories (e.g. La Via AVM, every
       image's Category left null) has nothing to show cards for, so it
       keeps the plain merged grid below instead, exactly as it did before
       this section existed. *@
    @if (Model.GalleryCategories.Count > 0)
    {
        <div class="project-gallery-category-picker" data-gallery-category-picker>
            <div class="project-gallery-category-track" data-gallery-category-track>
                @foreach (var category in Model.GalleryCategories)
                {
                    var firstCategoryImage = Model.GalleryImages.FirstOrDefault(image => string.Equals(image.Category, category.Value, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));

                    <button type="button"
                            class="gallery-card"
                            data-gallery-category-card="@category.Label">
                        @if (firstCategoryImage is not null)
                        {
                            <img class="gallery-card-image" src="@firstCategoryImage.ThumbnailSrc" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                        }
                        <span class="gallery-card-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="gallery-card-title">@category.Label</span>
                    </button>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    var galleryBlocks = Model.GalleryImages
        .Where(image => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(image.Block))
        .Select(image => image.Block!)
        .Distinct()
        .ToList();
    var galleryApartmentTypes = Model.GalleryImages
        .Where(image => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(image.ApartmentType))
        .Select(image => image.ApartmentType!)
        .Distinct()
        .ToList();

    @if (galleryBlocks.Count > 0)
    {
        <div class="project-gallery-chip-row" data-gallery-block-row>
            @foreach (var block in galleryBlocks)
            {
                <button type="button" class="project-gallery-chip" data-gallery-block-chip="@block">@block</button>
            }
        </div>
    }
    @if (galleryApartmentTypes.Count > 0)
    {
        <div class="project-gallery-chip-row" data-gallery-apartment-row hidden>
            @foreach (var apartmentType in galleryApartmentTypes)
            {
                <button type="button" class="project-gallery-chip" data-gallery-apartment-chip="@apartmentType">@apartmentType</button>
            }
        </div>
    }

    <div class="project-gallery-cards" data-gallery-cards data-reveal-group @(Model.GalleryCategories.Count > 0 ? "hidden" : null)>
        @if (Model.GalleryCategories.Count > 0)
        {
            @foreach (var category in Model.GalleryCategories)
            {
                var categoryImages = Model.GalleryImages
                    .Where(image => string.Equals(image.Category, category.Value, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                    .ToList();
                var groupKey = "gallery-" + category.Value.ToLowerInvariant().Replace(" ", "-");

                for (var i = 0; i < categoryImages.Count; i++)
                {
                    var image = categoryImages[i];

                    @if (image.VideoUrl is not null)
                    {
                        @* Gallery video card (Gallery video support, 2026-08-09)
                           — same card shell as a photo, poster thumbnail only
                           (no <video> element here), Play opens the shared
                           video modal (#concept-video-modal, site.js) instead
                           of the Media Viewer — mirrors _ProjectConcept.cshtml's
                           own video-slide branch exactly. Never carries
                           data-media-viewer-* — the Media Viewer is image-only. *@
                        <button type="button"
                                class="gallery-card gallery-card--video"
                                data-reveal
                                data-gallery-category="@category.Label"
                                data-gallery-block="@image.Block"
                                data-gallery-apartment-type="@image.ApartmentType"
                                data-gallery-video-play
                                data-video-src="@image.VideoUrl"
                                data-poster-src="@image.Src"
                                data-video-title="@image.Alt"
                                aria-label="@($"{image.Alt} videosunu oynat")">
                            <img class="gallery-card-image" src="@image.ThumbnailSrc" alt="@image.Alt" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                            <span class="gallery-card-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="gallery-card-play" aria-hidden="true">
                                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true">
                                    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
                                    <path d="M10 8l6 4-6 4V8z" fill="currentColor" />
                                </svg>
                            </span>
                            <span class="gallery-card-title">@category.Label</span>
                        </button>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <button type="button"
                                class="gallery-card"
                                data-reveal
                                data-gallery-category="@category.Label"
                                data-gallery-block="@image.Block"
                                data-gallery-apartment-type="@image.ApartmentType"
                                data-media-viewer-trigger
                                data-media-viewer-group="gallery-all"
                                data-media-viewer-group-category="@groupKey"
                                data-media-viewer-src="@image.Src"
                                data-media-viewer-alt="@image.Alt"
                                aria-label="@($"{category.Label} — büyüt")">
                            <img class="gallery-card-image" src="@image.ThumbnailSrc" alt="@image.Alt" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                            <span class="gallery-card-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="gallery-card-title">@category.Label</span>
                        </button>
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        else
        {
            @* No named categories at all (e.g. La Via AVM — every image's
               Category is null, see BuildKuyuluAvmImages) — every image
               renders as one ungrouped set, same card markup minus the
               per-category title overlay, since there is no category name to
               show. The dropdown above still renders (Options is empty), so
               its menu offers only _FilterDropdown's built-in "Tüm
               Görseller" entry. *@
            for (var i = 0; i < Model.GalleryImages.Count; i++)
            {
                var image = Model.GalleryImages[i];
                var accessibleLabel = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(image.Alt) ? $"Galeri görseli {i + 1}" : image.Alt;

                <button type="button"
                        class="gallery-card"
                        data-reveal
                        data-media-viewer-trigger
                        data-media-viewer-group="gallery-all"
                        data-media-viewer-group-category="gallery-all"
                        data-media-viewer-src="@image.Src"
                        data-media-viewer-alt="@image.Alt"
                        aria-label="@($"{accessibleLabel} — büyüt")">
                    <img class="gallery-card-image" src="@image.ThumbnailSrc" alt="@image.Alt" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                    <span class="gallery-card-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </button>
            }
        }
    </div>

    <div class="project-gallery-nav-group" @(Model.GalleryCategories.Count > 0 ? "hidden" : null)>
        <button type="button" class="history-nav-btn project-gallery-nav project-gallery-prev" data-gallery-prev aria-label="Önceki görsel">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="history-nav-btn project-gallery-nav project-gallery-next" data-gallery-next aria-label="Sonraki görsel">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </div>
}
